      "valuation_insights": "Apple Inc. reported total revenue of $478.8 billion for fiscal year 2026 [C:revenue2026]. This represents a year-over-year growth of about 15.06% compared to $416.2 billion in fiscal 2025 [C:revenue_growth2026]. Operating income was $158.1 billion, yielding an operating margin of approximately 33.0% for the year [C:operating_income2026] [C:operating_margin2026]. Net income attributable to the company amounted to $132.2 billion [C:net_income2026], with GAAP diluted earnings per share of $8.98 [C:diluted_eps2026]. The return on average equity stood at about 142.3% [C:return_on_average_equity2026]. Debt to equity ratio, including the current portion of debt, was roughly 0.70 [C:debt_to_equity2026]. Free cash flow, calculated as operating cash flow less capital expenditures, was $136.1 billion [C:free_cash_flow2026].\n\nFor the latest quarter ended September 26, 2026, Apple posted revenue of $114.5 billion, up 12% year-over-year [C:latest_quarter_revenue]. The GAAP diluted EPS for this quarter was $2.10 [C:latest_quarter_eps]. Based on the closing stock price of $344.63 on October 30, 2026, the price-to-earnings ratio derived from fiscal 2026 GAAP diluted EPS is approximately 38.38 [C:pe_ratio].\n\nIn comparison to its peers, Apple's operating margin of 33.0% is below Microsoft Corp's 46.8% [C:msft_operating_margin], above Alphabet Inc.'s 32.0% [C:googl_operating_margin], and above Oracle Corp's 30.6% [C:orcl_operating_margin]. All peer operating margins are based on a consistent total-revenue definition.\n",
